UID:27635-1791059400-1791059400@www.lotusfest.org
SUMMARY:Parade Through the Lights
DESCRIPTION:Date: October 3rd\nTime: 8:30 PM\nLocation: Courthouse Square\nTo start the parade: Meet up behind Fountain Square Mall on 4th St next to WFHB! \nAs the sun sets and the lanterns begin to glow\, the Lotus Festival Parade invites the community to step into a living work of art. Led by the spirit of Lotus and brought to life through music\, dance\, movement\, and imagination\, this illuminated procession transforms downtown into a celebration of connection and creativity. \nGuided by the warm light of the Trail of Luminaria\, participants and spectators alike will journey together through a night filled with rhythm\, color\, and wonder. From handmade lanterns to spontaneous joy\, every light and every person becomes part of the story. \nAll are welcome. All are needed. Whether you dance\, carry a lantern\, create art\, volunteer\, or simply walk beside us\, your presence helps brighten the path forward. \nInterested in joining the effort\, volunteering\, or partnering?\nEmail KP at associatedirector@lotusfest.org and share your light. \nParade Map
URL:https://www.lotusfest.org/event/parade-through-the-lights-2026/
CATEGORIES:Free Event,Lotus Festival,Arts Activity
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://www.lotusfest.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Site-Event-Images-2.webp
END:VEVENT
