UID:28148-1791104400-1791115200@www.lotusfest.org
SUMMARY:Festival Unwind Yoga
DESCRIPTION:$10 donation suggested at the door. Limited tickets available! \nThe event is at Nourishing Heart Studio. \nStudents of all levels are welcome to join these accessible practices and are encouraged to work at their own pace. Participants may drop in or leave as they choose. Multiple teachers will be on hand to demonstrate. Lotus Festival artists are invited to participate in these yoga sessions along with Festival patrons and the general public. All voluntary donations support Lotus Blossoms Education & Outreach programs and Lotus Education and Arts Foundation. \nOrder Tickets \n9–9:50 a.m. — Slow Flow with Live Acoustic Sound\nWith Matece Skow and Sarah Flint\nA grounding\, spacious practice accompanied by live acoustic music—a gentle continuation of the Festival experience. \n10–10:50 a.m. — Rhythm & Roots: An All-Levels Community Flow\nA joyful\, accessible practice set to music from around the world. Move\, breathe\, and reconnect in a class celebrating rhythm\, community\, and our shared humanity. \n11 a.m.–11:50 a.m. — Soulful Soundscape\nWith Jill Courtney\nImmersive sound from various instruments and crystal bowls invite the body to soften\, the nervous system to settle\, and the Festival weekend to come to a deeply restful close.
URL:https://www.lotusfest.org/event/festival-unwind-yoga-2026/
LOCATION:Nourishing Heart Studio\, 582 E Hillside Dr #1\, Bloomington\, IN\, 47401\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.lotusfest.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/yoga-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
